# CMake / build directories
build/
bin/
lib/
*.obj
*.pdb
*.ilk
*.exp

# Deployed plugin binaries are build outputs (rebuilt by PluginBuilder / CMake), not sources.
# Keep the folder so the .toe can find the plugin path; DLLs are regenerated by a build.
__Plugins__/**/*.dll
__Plugins__/**/*.dll.old*
*.dll.old*

# The oneMKL runtime, when it is deployed next to FFT.dll so the FFT Backend toggle works in
# TouchDesigner: the plugin resolves the library from its own directory (pluginDirectory() in
# FftBackend.h), so `__Plugins__/FFT/` is the only place it can live at run time. It is 521 MB and
# entirely optional - the plugin runs on the vendored FFTW3 with none of it present - so it is never
# vendored here, only staged by hand for the machine that wants it. The notices *are* kept with it,
# because the Intel Simplified Software License requires the license text and the third-party
# notices to travel with a redistribution of the DLLs:
#   https://github.com/NairoDorian/TD_Custom_FFT -> 3rdParty/fftw3/README.md, "Using Intel oneMKL"
__Plugins__/FFT/oneMKL-licenses/

# Vendored FFTW: only the single-precision runtime + import lib are needed
PluginProjects/FFT/3rdParty/fftw3/temp_extract/
PluginProjects/FFT/3rdParty/fftw3/*.zip
# A vendored library that is not in the repository is not vendored: the rules above exclude the
# `bin/` and `lib/` *directories* at any depth, and git cannot re-include a file whose parent
# directory was excluded - so the negations that used to sit here (naming libfftw3f-3.dll, the
# previous version's file) never took effect. A fresh clone had no FFTW DLL and could not build.
# Un-excluding the two directories first is what makes the per-file rules below actually work;
# `git check-ignore -v <path>` is how to confirm it after any edit to this file.
!PluginProjects/FFT/3rdParty/fftw3/bin/
!PluginProjects/FFT/3rdParty/fftw3/lib/
!PluginProjects/FFT/3rdParty/fftw3/bin/libfftw3f-*.dll
!PluginProjects/FFT/3rdParty/fftw3/lib/libfftw3f-*.def
!PluginProjects/FFT/3rdParty/fftw3/lib/libfftw3f-*.lib
# The .exp is a byproduct of generating the .lib from the .def (ignored globally above), and the
# runtime DLL is kept in bin/ only - CMake stages it from there, so lib/ holds no second copy.

# Visual Studio / VS Code / IDE temporary files
.vs/
launch.vs.json.user
CMakeUserPresets.json
compile_commands.json

# Backup files
*.bckp
.bckp/
Backup/
Plugin_FFT.[0-9]*.toe
*.[0-9]*.toe

# Command Code tool configuration / scratch
.commandcode/
scratchpad/

# OS metadata
# Build helper / test artifacts (per-project)
PluginProjects/FFT/_b.bat
PluginProjects/FFT/_c.bat
PluginProjects/FFT/fft_tests_wisdom.txt

# OS metadata
Thumbs.db
Desktop.ini
.DS_Store

# The DSP tests cache wisdom next to wherever they are run from; only the project-root copy is tracked.
fft_tests_wisdom.txt
